config BR2_PACKAGE_LEDS_GPIO_CUSTOM_DRIVER
	bool "leds-gpio-custom-driver"
	depends on BR2_LINUX_KERNEL
	help
	  Production-ready LED class driver using standard Linux LED subsystem.
	  
	  This driver provides a proper LED class implementation following
	  mainline kernel standards. It exposes LEDs through /sys/class/leds/
	  interface with support for:
	  
	  - Standard LED triggers (heartbeat, timer, oneshot, etc.)
	  - Brightness control (0-255)
	  - Hardware blinking support
	  - Power management (suspend/resume)
	  - Device Tree configuration
	  - Runtime parameter override via DT overlays
	  
	  The driver is designed for GPIO-controlled LEDs and follows
	  kernel conventions including devm_* resource management,
	  proper error handling, and maintainable code structure.
	  
	  Features:
	  * LED class subsystem integration (/sys/class/leds/)
	  * GPIO descriptor API for modern GPIO handling
	  * Device Tree bindings with runtime overlay support
	  * Hardware blinking support via set_brightness_blocking
	  * Proper power management (suspend/resume)
	  * UAPI header for userspace applications
	  * Comprehensive documentation
	  
	  Compared to the legacy gpio_chardev driver (Lộ trình 3), this driver
	  follows the production-ready approach (Lộ trình 2) recommended for
	  mainline kernel submission.
	  
	  https://github.com/yourusername/leds-gpio-custom
